cm of the deep inked margin  3 0cm of the lateral margin  4 0cm of the inferior margin  and 5 0cm of the medial margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with interculating fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  several lymph nodes are identified  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing one lymph node  The node is bisected and submitted in S  SECTION CODE  A C  biopsy site with superior margin and skin  D  biopsy site with superior margin  E G  biopsy site with deep inked margin  H  lateral margin  I  inferior margin  J  medial margin  K  nipple  L N  lymph nodes  low  O P  lymph nodes  middle  Q R  lymph nodes  high  S  lymph node  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Craig Scott Seidman  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY NODE  LEFT    report_end  , Mastectomy.
