rgin and measuring 0 6cm from the posterior resection margin  and 0 8cm from the anterior resection margin  No axillary lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   firm area to the anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   firm area to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   region of calcifications   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   area of calcifications and faintly blue spherical cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   additional probable cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   additional probable cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   ropey fibrous area and probable cyst to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative fibrous areas  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 12 x 3 cm left simple mastectomy with a stitch designating 6 oclock  The anterior is inked blue  and the posterior is inked black  The overlying 3 3 cm diameter areola contains a central 1 2 cm diameter nipple  The nipple areola complex is grossly unremarkable  Sectioning of the specimen reveals a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9 cm well defined  transparent fibrous area located 2 8cm from the lateral edge and measuring 0 9cm from the anterior margin and 1 0cm from the posterior margin  consistent with previous biopsy site  The breast tissue in the inferior part of the breast  medial to the biopsy site  appears thin and atrophic  while the remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  No axillary lymph nodes are present  Also received in the container is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3 cm strip of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  the skin surface is pink  containing rare hairs  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   biopsy site to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   section surrounding biopsy site   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   section of biopsy site to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   section of gritty  fibrous tissue to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_