Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 48 CLINICAL DATA  53 year old female status post chemotherapy for stage III breast carcinoma  She now undergoes right modified mastectomy and axillary node dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  99   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1    SEE NOTE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN SEVEN OF EIGHTEEN AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  7 18   NOTE  The carcinoma is 0 4cm from the closest deep resection margin  Lymphatic invasion is present  The nipple skin is not involved by carcinoma  The tumor appears viable  Diagnosis by  Robert B  Colvin  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 43                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with overall dimensions of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  The overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 11 5cm  The nipple is 5 0cm from the inferior skin margin and 8 3cm from the medial skin margin  On sectioning through the breast  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 8cm hard  stellate region with bands of white fibrous tissue intermixed  as well as  areas that have the appearance of fat necrosis  This region is beneath the 4 0cm curvilinear healed biopsy skin scar that is 2 0cm superior to the nipple  The stellate region is 0 6cm from the closest deep margin  4 8cm from the closest inferior margin and 3 2cm from the closest superior margin  Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  These range in size from 0 1cm in diameter up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Some of these nodes are grossly positive  SECTION CODE  A D  tumor and closest deep margin  radial EandF  nipple G  tissue beneath nipple H  upper medial quadrant  representative I  lower medial quadrant  representative J  upper outer quadrant  representative K  lower outer quadrant  representative L R  axillary lymph nodes  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Mastectomy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 32 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CONFINED TO THE MASS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a breast lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm containing two sutures  A short suture designates the superior margin and a long suture designates the lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 3cm hemorrhagic biopsy site with an adjacent 1 4cm firm  tan white area grossly abutting the inked margins anteriorly  The biopsy site comes within 1 5cm of the deep margin which is overinked blue  The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is composed predominantly of dense  white  fibrous tissue with no additional anomalies  SECTION CODE A  FX  1  residue  B C  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest anterior margin  D  Biopsy cavity in relation to deep margin  inked blue   E  Remainder of biopsy cavity with adjacent firm nodule abutting anterior margin  F  Representative section of fibrous tissue from medial aspect  G  Representative section of fibrous tissue from lateral aspect  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are 3 additional specimens  Labeled  additional shaved margins  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  The specimens are sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes H through M  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a segment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted entirely in cassette N and O  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm segment of fatty adipose tissue  Numerous lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes P through S  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST LUMPECTOMY   MARGIN FREE OF TUMOR   NO TUMOR IN THE SECTION   O R  Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGINS   EXCISIO PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL    EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
