Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 17 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast re excision positive margins on outside lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU SINGLE IACROSCOPIC FOCUS   0 05 CM  PRESENT IN THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND EXTENDS TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 39                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm of irregular tan yellow to pink fibrofatty tissue with a long suture designating the new medial margin and a short suture designating the superior aspect  Along the anterior aspect there is a 3 05cm in length and 0 3cm in diameter unremarkable tan white portion of skin  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  the medial green and the lateral yellow  The specimen is sequentially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm empty cavity which communicates with the infero anterior aspect  The cavity lining is pink to white  smooth to roughened and focally hemorrhagic  The borders are tan pink  rubbery and ragged with well circumscribed chalky tan yellow areas  consistent with fat necrosis  The surrounding tissue is predominantly dense  rubbery unremarkable fibrous tissue  The cavity comes to 0 5cm from the posterior aspect  0 6cm from the lateral  2 0cm from the medial  0 7cm from the superior and 0 5cm from the inferior aspect  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A J with the cavity in cassettes A H and uninvolved fibrous tissue in cassettes I J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast final shave margins  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular tan yellow to pink unoriented portion of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to display a tan yellow to pink unremarkable cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes K R  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SGR                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA  The patient has a left breast mass and a clinically palpable axillary node                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE SPINDLE CELL CARCINOMA  METAPLASTIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1    SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunostains performed on frozen sections and paraffin embedded sections of the tumor and lymph node metastasis are negative for AEI 3 CAM  EMA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   WS keratin and desmin  Vimentin stains are positive  In view of the presence of high grade carcinoma in situ  the diagnosis of spindle cell carcinoma  metaplastic mammary carcinoma is favored  The excisional biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   did not contain any ductal carcinoma in situ  hence the diagnosis of sarcoma was considered  This case has been reviewed by Drs  A  Rosenberg and F  Koerner  who concur with the diagnosis  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE   METASTATIC TUMOR IN REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES  ALMOST COMPLETELY REPLACING THE NODE  AND MEASURING REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 15 27 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block U   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 41     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum          ELECTRON MICROSCOPY ADDENDUM    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        BREAST TUMOR   SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM WITH FEATURES SUGGESTIVE OF FIBROBLASTIC DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tissue was formalin fixed and is not optimally preserved  The tumor cells are embedded in extracellular collagenous matrix  They are cohesive and intercellular junctions are prominent  The cytoplasm has an admixture of dilated and non dilated rough endoplasmic reticulum  free ribosomes  mitochondria and filaments  No definitive features of epithelial differentiation are seen  The findings are consistent with a mesenchymal neoplasm  however  similar ultrastructural features can be seen in sarcomatoid carcinoma  which cannot be excluded  Added by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of breast with a REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm unremarkable tan skin ellipse and an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  Specimen is black inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm white gritty well delineated mass located 2 0cm from the deep and 2 5cm from the skin margins  The remaining parenchyma is 90  yellow lobulated fatty tissue and 10  thin white fibrous tissue surface  Within the attached axillary tail are multiple tan pink rubbery lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm to 4 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative section of tumor is saved frozen  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A 