Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 03 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 03 at 09 05 CLINICAL DATA  Positive margins on lumpectomy  Left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 2 of 6 blocks  E and F   Spanning at least 0 8cm  Grade  2 Calcifications  Limited to the carcinoma in situ Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  in the most lateral portion of the specimen  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 03 at 18 05                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision short stitch superior  long stitch lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The posterior margin is inked green  the anterior yellow  the superior black  and the inferior blue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm exposed cavity along the anterior aspect  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal focal hemorrhage and extensive tan yellow areas consistent with fat necrosis surrounding the cavity  Along the anterior half of the specimen there is a fairly well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm indurated gray white lesion which communicates with the cavity  focally abuts the a