d blue and the posterior margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm hemorrhagic biopsy cavity  containing red fluid  The cavity is lined by focal areas of dense  white fibrous tissue  with no discrete masses or lesions identified  The cavity is 1 8cm from the posterior margin and underlies the previously described well healed scar  The remaining cut surface displays focal areas of dense  white fibrous tissue with no masses or lesion identified  No lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sequential cross sections of biopsy cavity  from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue which may represent lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of unoriented yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimens are inked black and serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of yellow lobulated adipose tissue  in which a 3 0cm in greatest dimension pink to yellow  rubbery lymph node is identified  The lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast lateral additional tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm aggregate of unoriented yellow lobulated adipose tissue  which is inked black and seri