 filled biopsy cavities directly beneath the recent surgical incisions  The medial located biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and is surrounded by firm  grey white  and focally yellow tissue  This cavity comes within 1 0cm of the superior medial inked resection margin  and 2 2cm from the deep resection margin  The lateral biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  and is surrounded by firm  white  focally yellow tissue  This biopsy cavity comes to within 0 3cm of the deep resection margin  and 1 3cm from the lateral superior resection margin  Remaining breast parenchyma is predominantly soft yellow adipose tissue  with occasional white fibrous strands  No suspicious lesions are identified  Numerous semifirm  tan  lymph nodes are present in the axillary tail  and measure from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest dimension  SECTION CODE  A  medial biopsy cavity  in relation to inked superior medial resection margin B  medial biopsy cavity  in relation to inked deep resection margin C E  representative sections of medial biopsy cavity F H  lateral biopsy cavity in relation to inked deep resection margin I  lateral biopsy cavity in relation to inked superior lateral resection margin J  lateral biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin with healing incision  and inked superior lateral resection margin K  medial biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin  recent biopsy incision and inked superior medial resection margin L  representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma from lateral breast M  representative section of nipple and areola N P  axillary lymph nodes  Labeled  axillary contents   are two fragments of soft  yellow adipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Three semifirm  tan to purple lymph nodes  measuring from 0 6cm to 2 5cm in greatest dimension are dissected from the adipose tissue and submitted in Q  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD              